(Q3: Define Gross Domestic Product \(GDP\).) Tj
/F1 9 Tf
0 -13 Td
(Ans: GDP is the total monetary value of all the finished goods and services produced within the domestic territory of a country during a specific period of time \(normally one year\). [2 Marks]) Tj
0 -13 Td
0 -8 Td
/F1 9.5 Tf
(Q4: What are the fundamental rights guaranteed by the Indian Constitution?) Tj
/F1 9 Tf
0 -13 Td
(Ans: 1. Right to Equality, 2. Right to Freedom, 3. Right against Exploitation, 4. Right to Freedom of Religion, 5. Cultural and Educational Rights, 6. Right to Constitutional Remedies. [2 Marks]) Tj
0 -13 Td
0 -8 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(### 5 Marks Essay Question) Tj
/F1 9 Tf
0 -15 Td
/F1 9.5 Tf
(Q5: Explain the salient features of the Constitution of India.) Tj
/F1 9 Tf
0 -13 Td
(Ans: Step 1: Lengthiest Written Constitution: Most detailed constitution in the world with Preamble, Articles, Parts, and Schedules. [1 Mark]) Tj
0 -13 Td
(Step 2: Blend of Rigidity and Flexibility: Some provisions require special parliamentary majority, others require simple majority. [1 Mark]) Tj
0 -12 Td
(Step 3: Federal System with Unitary Bias: Dual government structure with strong central power during emergencies. [1 Mark]) Tj
0 -12 Td
(Step 4: Secular State & Universal Adult Suffrage: No state religion; equal voting rights for all citizens aged 18 and above without discrimination. [1 Mark]) Tj
0 -12 Td
(Step 5: Independent Judiciary & Fundamental Rights: Single integrated judicial system with Supreme Court as guardian of rights. [1 Mark]) Tj
0 -12 Td
